HID: sony: send SHANWAN output reports over the control channel on BT

The SHANWAN_GAMEPAD quirk routes LED/rumble output reports through the
interrupt channel. The SHANWAN PS3 clones used by RGM drop the Bluetooth
link within a second of receiving that packet (btmon: pad answers with a
spurious handshake and sends L2CAP Disconnection Requests). Delivering the
same report as a SET_REPORT on the control channel keeps them connected,
which was verified by renaming the device so the quirk did not match.
Keep the interrupt path for USB, where the quirk was introduced.

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
@@ -1512,8 +1512,12 @@ static void sixaxis_send_output_report(struct sony_sc *sc)
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* SHANWAN controllers require output reports via intr channel */
-	if (sc->quirks & SHANWAN_GAMEPAD)
+	/*
+	 * SHANWAN controllers require output reports via intr channel on USB,
+	 * but over Bluetooth they disconnect on intr data; use SET_REPORT.
+	 */
+	if ((sc->quirks & SHANWAN_GAMEPAD) &&
+	    !(sc->quirks & SIXAXIS_CONTROLLER_BT))
 		hid_hw_output_report(sc->hdev, (u8 *)report,
 				sizeof(struct sixaxis_output_report));
 	else
